{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/688941-crossover-question-gaian-shapechangers-and-unseelie-fae","id":688941,"title":"Crossover Question Gaian Shapechangers And Unseelie fae.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-04T15:53:42-07:00","id":688941,"title":"Crossover Question Gaian Shapechangers And Unseelie fae.","content":"Is it unbelievable For Garou to knowingly treat with the unseelie, or are unseelie inherently &quot;Of the wyrm&quot;<br /> <br /> House balor rather patently is, but house Ailil I could see being smiled on by some shadow lords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T16:17:56-07:00","id":688986,"title":"","content":"House Balor claims Lugh and Cuchulainn as members by descent, however, so it's not so clear cut (both are revered by the Fianna, though the Fianna don't exactly have the best track record at discerning what would be a good ally). In general, Thallain are almost certain to be jerks, assholes, or perhaps even 100% dicks, but that alone doesn't necessarily make them a being of elemental corruption. Above all else, Changelings, unseelie or otherwise, are seen as unreliable by most Garou and Fera, on account of how they can potentially end up making deals, then succumbing to Banality or chimerical death and forgetting some very vital points regarding their agreements, which is almost certainly going to be handled with the degree of compassion and understanding that one usually expects of mob legbreakers, followed by a strong aversion toward future dealings with changelings in the sept for a long time after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T16:39:27-07:00","id":689005,"title":"","content":"To frame my response, I am not a changeling person, never understood the appeal of the game. That said, based on everything I have read, I don't see anything outwardly that links them directly to the Wyrm. According to the book &quot;The Shadow Court&quot;, the Fianna deal with the Seelie mostly but those of a less traditionalist nature have been known to deal with the Unseelie on occasion. The Shadow lords had also been known to make brief alliances with the Unseelie, but both sides don't trust one another and are likely to betray the other so their alliances don't tend to last long. House Balor and the Black Spiral Dancers have a long standing alliance with one another (Which used to be reflected in the BSD gift Unseelie Faerie Kin, not sure if that one is still around).<br /> <br /> All in all most of the Changing Breeds do not like to deal with the Fae, most don't trust them and their reputation among them has been justly earned. If I remember correctly, the Get of Fenris kill both sides indiscriminately for some slight they Fae made on them in the bronze age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T16:59:11-07:00","id":689015,"title":"","content":"oh an idea I had come into my head?<br /> <br /> A Fianna sells some DNA Prisoners to Some unseelie as slaves.<br /> <br /> IT gets him some money and as the garou dont have space for POW Camps, is possibly the best option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T17:46:20-07:00","id":689040,"title":"","content":"Why are the Fianna taking prisoners? And why are they selling slaves? Slavery is the perfect environment for the Wyrm to fester and grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T17:55:38-07:00","id":689043,"title":"","content":"Well what better use for DNA People?<br /> <br /> Then again, played in 2 separate games where DNA Agents were given a slap on the wrist and let go...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T18:44:53-07:00","id":689082,"title":"","content":"For the most part we have always found their best use to be fertilizer. In rare occasion slap on the wrist for those that really believe they are trying to help. The former more then the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T20:11:14-07:00","id":689135,"title":"","content":"Unseelie fae are a natural part of the world. They are not considered to be of the Wyrm. However, those Unseelie of the Shadow Court seem to serve some sort of force that the Garou would recognize as belonging to the Wyrm. And there are probably other stories of individual Fae serving the Wyrm just like any other people in the world.<br /> <br /> For the most part, I don't think Garou would make any distinction or treat them any different unless there is additional information that would cause them to be suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T00:47:52-07:00","id":689400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/688941-crossover-question-gaian-shapechangers-and-unseelie-fae?p=689015#post689015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh an idea I had come into my head?<br /> <br /> A Fianna sells some DNA Prisoners to Some unseelie as slaves.<br /> <br /> IT gets him some money and as the garou dont have space for POW Camps, is possibly the best option.</div> </div> </div> </div>What. What!? Why would a Garou ever consider something like that? Where is the Honor, Glory or Wisdom in that? I could see a Black Spiral Dancer doing it, but a Fianna never would. Garou don't have POW camps. They either kill you or let you live. They do not have the resources or the time to do anything else.<br /> <br /> The concept itself makes me cringe and stare at screen wondering if you ever actually read a Werewolf book.<br /> <br /> Also, you may be quite pushing the courts and the nebulous ties the Fianna have with Fae. Note that their tie is with Fae creatures, not the Courts of Changeling specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T01:11:12-07:00","id":689435,"title":"","content":"have read many books and your right This is probaly just some of my Anger at seeing DNA people let loose with a slap on the wrists. and Im like... &quot;Uhmmmn... what?&quot; <br /> <br /> your right its probaly uncharachteristic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T02:40:48-07:00","id":689516,"title":"","content":"Delete your busted sig, no one cares what you back. You know there is a difference between reading a book and comprehending what you read. Given the bulk of the threads you start I'm pretty sure its the former not the later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachment